{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339149-why-can-t-you-reach-to-make-scale-primary-spell-factor","id":1339149,"title":"Why can't you reach to make Scale Primary spell factor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-03T02:47:21-07:00","id":1339149,"title":"Why can't you reach to make Scale Primary spell factor?","content":"What's the reason behind Potency and Duration being the only two Primary spell factors. While it makes sense that they're the &quot;most default&quot;, why can't +Reach option switch it over to Scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:42:25-07:00","id":1339205,"title":"","content":"Because that\u2019s what the devs decided.<br /> <br /> Which probably isn\u2019t a satisfying answer, but it\u2019s the only non-speculative one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T16:28:02-07:00","id":1339258,"title":"","content":"Unless somewhere some dev has mentioned this, and someone knows exactly why. Anyways, yes, that's my question, why they decided that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:20:05-07:00","id":1339268,"title":"","content":"None of the fans know outside of speculating. Try getting in touch with DaveB as the developer that decided it and the primary person to clarify this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T19:02:35-07:00","id":1339741,"title":"","content":"Of course, this is all speculation, but...<br /> The guidelines for determining the primary factor of a spell are fuzzy, but the logic is that the platonic ideal of the spell would have an infinite value in that factor. A damage spell would kill anything with health levels. A spell with no use for extra Potency would last forever. Sometimes it can get tricky: you can argue that a spell that gives extra dice or dots would be &quot;more better&quot; if it gave an infinite amount of dice/dots, but it also would be next to useless or at least of very limited use if it only lasts for a single turn, while a spell that grants a single die/dot forever is definitely useful. Some Spells may, in the abstract, look like affecting a bigger or more targets would be a more powerful version of the spell, like Ward or Teleportation, but when you consider the other game mechanics, like Clash of Wills and Sympathy and Withstand, you notice that it actually makes way more sense to have a higher Duration or Potency respectively. And so, since no spell would have Scale as its primary factor by default, it makes sense then that you can't Reach to make it so.<br /> <br /> House ruling it shouldn't be that big of a deal, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T08:07:02-07:00","id":1340227,"title":"","content":"I guess I've been running things wrong because I have been letting a Reach change the primary spell factor to any of the factors. It just hasn't come up a lot. Does it actually say somewhere those are the only two choices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T09:02:33-07:00","id":1340240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1339149-why-can-t-you-reach-to-make-scale-primary-spell-factor?p=1340227#post1340227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I've been running things wrong because I have been letting a Reach change the primary spell factor to any of the factors. It just hasn't come up a lot. Does it actually say somewhere those are the only two choices?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;All spells have a primary spell factor of either Potency or Duration.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T09:16:04-07:00","id":1340241,"title":"","content":"Page 113: &quot;All spells have a <b>primary spell factor </b>of either Potency or Duration.&quot;<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that making Range and Casting Time a primary factor would literally have no effect. There is no base value to increase based on the highest Arcanum used. So using Reach to make either of this primary would be completely pointless.<br /> <br /> I can't really see anyone ever paying a Reach to make Scale primary given the comparative math of using that Reach to make it Advanced Scale instead. There's maybe a few outlier spells where Potency and Duration at low levels are worth it, but in the vast majority of cases, using that Reach to bump Scale to Advanced and taking maybe a -2 or -4 if you really need to impact a lot of people, is going to be less than the dice penalties you'll take to bump up Potency and/or Duration for the Scale to really matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T11:51:59-07:00","id":1340654,"title":"","content":"I can see some cases where you might want it, like if you want a scene long Shielding spell on your whole Cabal, or stuff like that where Potency is not very useful, and you are fine just the first step of Advanced Duration. Or when you already want Advanced Scale but it it's still not enough with just one step, like if you want a to affect a really big building or the biggest storm you can make, or even affecting something really big like a plane or train (for affecting it directly, like with a Forces spell, not the people inside).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T13:39:15-07:00","id":1342397,"title":"","content":"I think its because it can get mechanically confusing. Imagine your spell hits a target, they withstand it, so lets say this makes it shrink to a size where the target is no longer within range. So now they aren't withstanding the spell, which means it shouldn't affect its size, right ? Since this can create a paradox, the easiest way to preserve clarity of the rules is to eliminate this edge case from the design space altogether. There is also the fact that multiple people withstanding it could decrease the range massively each time, barring an exceptional success bypassing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-19-2019, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}